From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Report a fixed NVIDIA adapter to D3DMetal, opt-in.

D3DMetal fills in the DXGI adapter description with a vendor of its own
choosing unless D3DM_VENDOR_ID, D3DM_DEVICE_ID and
D3DM_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION are set. They are read from the process
environment on the Unix side, which has not yet been confirmed end to
end. SetEnvironmentVariable() only changes the Windows environment and
does not reach them. Some programs take a vendor-specific path on
D3DMetal's default and fail there.

This adds an opt-in policy, read once at process start with the 0157
reader: HKCU\Software\Wine\AppDefaults\<app.exe>\Runeon, DWORD
D3DMetalReportNVIDIA = 1. With it, signal_init_process() sets
D3DM_VENDOR_ID=0x10de, D3DM_DEVICE_ID=0x2786 and
D3DM_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION="NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070" before any Windows
code runs and logs one RUNEON_D3DMETAL_ADAPTER line. If the caller has
set any of the three, the policy sets none, so an identity is never
mixed. The values are fixed in Wine; a launcher can only turn the policy
on for a program. A missing value, another type or value, or a failed
lookup leaves the environment unchanged. It is never keyed on a program
in Wine.

A child process inherits the Unix environment. So that one program's
policy does not reach its children, RUNEON_D3DM_SET records that the
policy set the variables, and every process drops them at start.
Reporting NVIDIA can open NVIDIA-only paths in a program, such as DLSS
or Reflex, that may then fail differently.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index f718d4b..cc3ce1c 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -1187,6 +1187,44 @@ static BOOL runeon_app_policy( const WCHAR *valueW )
 static const WCHAR rosetta_cpu_fidelityW[] = {'R','o','s','e','t','t','a','C','p','u','F','i','d','e','l','i','t','y',0};
 static const WCHAR metal_shader_cache_expandW[] =
     {'M','e','t','a','l','S','h','a','d','e','r','C','a','c','h','e','E','x','p','a','n','d',0};
+static const WCHAR d3dmetal_report_nvidiaW[] =
+    {'D','3','D','M','e','t','a','l','R','e','p','o','r','t','N','V','I','D','I','A',0};
+
+/* D3DMetal adapter identity (D3DMetalReportNVIDIA): D3DMetal takes
+ * D3DM_VENDOR_ID, D3DM_DEVICE_ID and D3DM_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION from the process
+ * environment on the Unix side, and otherwise reports a vendor of its own
+ * choosing; a program may then take a vendor-specific path that fails on
+ * D3DMetal. Report a fixed NVIDIA adapter instead, unless the caller has set any
+ * of the three, so an identity is never mixed. Child processes inherit the Unix
+ * environment, so RUNEON_D3DM_SET records that the policy set them, and each
+ * process drops them first: the policy of one program does not reach its
+ * children. */
+static void d3dmetal_adapter_policy(void)
+{
+    static const char * const vars[][2] =
+    {
+        { "D3DM_VENDOR_ID", "0x10de" },
+        { "D3DM_DEVICE_ID", "0x2786" },
+        { "D3DM_DEVICE_DESCRIPTION", "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070" },
+    };
+    unsigned int i;
+
+    if (getenv( "RUNEON_D3DM_SET" ))
+    {
+        for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(vars); i++) unsetenv( vars[i][0] );
+        unsetenv( "RUNEON_D3DM_SET" );
+    }
+    if (!runeon_app_policy( d3dmetal_report_nvidiaW )) return;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(vars); i++) if (getenv( vars[i][0] )) break;
+    if (i == ARRAY_SIZE(vars))
+    {
+        for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(vars); i++) setenv( vars[i][0], vars[i][1], 1 );
+        setenv( "RUNEON_D3DM_SET", "1", 1 );
+    }
+    FIXME_(seh)( "RUNEON_D3DMETAL_ADAPTER vendor=%s device=%s\n",
+                 debugstr_a( getenv( "D3DM_VENDOR_ID" )), debugstr_a( getenv( "D3DM_DEVICE_ID" )) );
+}
 
 /* Metal shader cache expansion (MetalShaderCacheExpand): Metal keeps the GPU
  * binaries it compiles in a per-process disk cache whose size it clamps to
@@ -3606,6 +3644,8 @@ void signal_init_process(void)
     }
     if (is_rosetta2 && runeon_app_policy( metal_shader_cache_expandW ))
         _dyld_register_func_for_add_image( metal_shader_cache_expand );
+    /* before D3DMetal is loaded; it reads the variables when an adapter is created */
+    d3dmetal_adapter_policy();
 #endif
 
     sig_act.sa_mask = server_block_set;
